emptyCallT -- SEQ 673 (Tony's ruling of 2026-11-16, F-161): on the new road f() is a call with no argument, as on the old.
incant/kantGrammar's INVOKEd took `EXPRESSIOn` inside the parentheses; it takes `EXPRESSIOn?`. INVOKEr builds the call
instruct with no third slot, and opCallTest hands the callee nothing. An empty subscript, a[], refuses by name.
Before: a new-road action body holding f() failed to build (ERROR processCode: <action> parse failed) and a STARt text
holding f() dropped its statement in silence.
Callers: o.. are old-road action bodies, n.. are new-road bodies (njNew), TOP is a STARt text run by testOP.
Callees: fz fb fh fi have old-road bodies; fzN fbN fhN are the same bodies built on the new road.
    a   fz() as a statement and inside an expression: "fz ran" twice, then 8.
    b   inside fb called as fb(): argument has no data (0) and prints its own name; @.taG reads fb.
    c   inside fb called as fb(ex): argument is ex (kind 5, value 5); @.taG reads ex.
    d   a C++ command called as dumpField(): it receives itself (it dumps "dumpField").
    h   fh's own name reads fh's attribute (red), called as fh() and as fh(ex).
    g   gB, a new-road action holding fbN(), with fbN and gB both compiled through the door (kwCompile): as the twin.
    f   an empty subscript. Old road: the action holding it fails to build, by name (ERROR processCode: oF). New road:
        REFUSED ea, by name, when the action or the STARt text is built; the statement after it is built and runs, as
        after any refused statement on the new road.
    i   MEASURE ONLY. box +% fi gives box a second field sharing fi's body. Inside fi, @.taG and this.taG, called fi(),
        fi(ex), box.fi(), box.fi(ex). The two fields have the same tag, so the tag cannot say which was called through.
A bare taG inside a NEW-road body reads 1, not the callee's tag, with f() and with f(x) alike (rows b and c, "callee
new"): the bare accessor on the new road, not the call. Pinned as it reads, not cured.
pop.sh runs this file twice: as written, and with the kwCompile( lines deleted (the twin). Stdout EC a OLD to EC END equal.
